    "description": "An island in the northern Black Sea at the mouth of the Borysthenes (Dnieper) river, settled by Milesian colonists in the late 7th century BC. It may have facilitated the foundation of the city of Olbia on the mainland. Conflict then arose between the two, and from the second half of the 5th century BC onwards, the island was an emporion of Olbia (itself often referred to as Borysthenes). In the Roman Imperial period, there was a cult of Achilles Pontarches on the island.",
    "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Berezan'</p>",
